.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.TH SP2P 1 "2025" "sp2p" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sp2p \- secure peer-to-peer file transfer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sp2p send
.RI [ flags ]
.IR file | folder | ... | \-
.br
.B sp2p receive
.RI [ flags ]
.I CODE
.br
.B sp2p version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sp2p
transfers files directly between two computers using WebRTC.
Files are end-to-end encrypted; the signaling server never sees file contents.
.PP
The sender generates a short code that the receiver enters to establish
a direct peer-to-peer connection.
If a direct connection cannot be established, a TURN relay is used
(with user confirmation unless
.B \-allow\-relay
is given).
.PP
For automation and AI agents, use
.B \-format json
to receive newline-delimited JSON lifecycle events. The sender's
.B session
event includes the transfer code; the final
.B result
event reports completion or failure. See
.I https://sp2p.io/llm
for the complete machine interface.
.PP
When direct connection fails, JSON mode emits a
.B relay_required
event containing the path of a temporary response file. Write
.B allow
or
.B deny
to that file to answer the relay prompt. The file is removed after it is read.
.PP
Healthy paused stdin and slow output finalization maintain peer heartbeats.
Physical network writes have a two-minute timeout; this is not an idle-stdin limit.
After sending Complete, a receiver waits at most five seconds for the final
shutdown acknowledgement. Verified published output is retained if it is lost.
.PP
Bootstrap scripts require no GitHub CLI. Shell downloads use curl or wget and
SHA-256 verification with sha256sum, shasum, or openssl (in that order);
PowerShell uses built-in commands. By default, if no supported verifier is
available, bootstrap stops without executing the CLI. The archive must match
the checksum manifest from the same fixed GitHub release before extraction.
This trusts the GitHub HTTPS release channel and bootstrap
host; it does not independently verify signer identity or prevent rollback.
.PP
To explicitly opt out, pass
.B \-\-insecure\-skip\-checksum
as the first argument to the downloaded shell or PowerShell bootstrap script,
before file paths, transfer codes, or CLI flags. This bootstrap-only option
skips manifest/hash checks, prints a warning to stderr, and runs downloaded
code without an archive integrity check. It is removed before invoking SP2P
and does not disable TLS certificate checks or release/platform URL validation.
It is not an option of the installed sp2p command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B send
Send one or more files or folders.
A share code is displayed for the receiver.
Use
.B \-
to read from stdin.
.TP
.B receive
Receive files using the share code provided by the sender.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and exit.
.SH SEND FLAGS
.TP
.BI \-compress " level"
zstd compression level, 0 to disable, 1\(en9 for increasing compression.
Default: 3.
.TP
.BI \-name " filename"
Filename to use when reading from stdin.
.TP
.B \-allow\-relay
Allow TURN relay connections without prompting.
.TP
.BI \-server " url"
Signaling server URL.
Default: value of
.B SP2P_SERVER
or
.IR http://localhost:8080 .
.TP
.BI \-url " url"
Public base URL for share links.
Default: value of
.B SP2P_URL
or the server URL.
.TP
.BI \-transport " mode"
Transport to use for the P2P connection.
Values:
.BR auto ", " tcp ", " webrtc .
Default:
.BR auto .
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose diagnostic output.
.TP
.BI \-format " format"
Output format:
.B human
or newline-delimited JSON events with
.BR json .
Default:
.BR human .
.TP
.BI \-event\-output " stream"
Where JSON events are written:
.B stdout
or
.BR stderr .
Default:
.BR stdout .
.TP
.BI \-status\-file " path"
Atomically write the latest private JSON status snapshot to
.IR path .
Requires
.BR \-format " json."
The snapshot includes the transfer code after session registration.
.SH RECEIVE FLAGS
.TP
.BI \-output " dir"
Output directory for received files.
Default:
.IR . " (current directory)."
.TP
.B \-stdout
Write received data to stdout instead of saving to a file.
.TP
.BI \-max\-receive\-bytes " bytes"
Maximum decoded transfer bytes, including unknown-size stdin.
Default: 0, meaning 1 TiB (1099511627776 bytes), not unlimited.
Use a larger positive finite byte count only for trusted transfers.
.TP
.BI \-max\-extract\-bytes " bytes"
Maximum expanded archive bytes, including sparse logical output.
Default: 0, meaning 1 TiB. Independent of the receive byte limit.
.TP
.B \-allow\-relay
Allow TURN relay connections without prompting.
.TP
.BI \-server " url"
Signaling server URL.
Default: value of
.B SP2P_SERVER
or
.IR http://localhost:8080 .
.TP
.BI \-transport " mode"
Transport to use for the P2P connection.
Values:
.BR auto ", " tcp ", " webrtc .
Default:
.BR auto .
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose diagnostic output.
.TP
.BI \-format " format"
Output format:
.B human
or newline-delimited JSON events with
.BR json .
Default:
.BR human .
.TP
.BI \-event\-output " stream"
Where JSON events are written:
.B stdout
or
.BR stderr .
Default:
.BR stdout .
When using
.BR \-stdout " to receive file bytes, set this to " stderr
so events do not corrupt the output.
.TP
.BI \-status\-file " path"
Atomically write the latest private JSON status snapshot to
.IR path .
Requires
.BR \-format " json."
.SH OUTPUT AND COMPATIBILITY
Transfer compatibility is automatic: two updated peers use v3, while
mixed 0.4.0/0.5.0 peers use v2. No version flag or browser checkbox is needed.
Both combinations work through either server version; signaling remains v2.
Clients and servers can be upgraded independently.
.PP
Capabilities are bound to key derivation and confirmation; tampering fails
authentication rather than silently downgrading updated peers.
Every v3 peer, including browsers, authenticates connection candidates and
sender selection. A server's claimed client type cannot disable authentication.
Connection errors never trigger a lower-version retry.
Legacy mode warns without prompting, omits v3 candidate authentication and
receiver credits, and disables parallel TCP even if a larger count was requested.
Updated peers retain local decoding, queue, quota, and output protections;
old peers retain their old vulnerabilities. Legacy idle/backpressure behavior
is weaker, and slow browser receivers can exceed their bounded input queues.
JSON mode emits a protocol event after key confirmation; subsequent events
and status snapshots report the authenticated version. Earlier records omit it.
.PP
Received content is verified, closed, and published before acknowledgement.
Existing files are not replaced; colliding file names receive an available
numbered name. Archives publish as one new directory, without merging into
existing output. A single matching folder keeps its root; multi-root archives
get a wrapper. Unsupported no-replace filesystems fail explicitly.
.PP
Close and publication do not guarantee power-loss durability. Stdout cannot
roll back bytes. A lost acknowledgement may leave valid committed output even
when the sender reports failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SP2P_SERVER
Signaling server URL (overridden by
.BR \-server ).
.TP
.B SP2P_URL
Public base URL for share links (overridden by
.BR \-url ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sp2p/config.yaml
User configuration file.
If
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set, defaults to
.IR ~/.config/sp2p/config.yaml .
.PP
The config file sets persistent defaults for command-line flags.
CLI flags and environment variables take precedence over config values.
.PP
Example config file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# Default signaling server
server: https://sp2p.example.com

# Public base URL for share links
url: https://sp2p.example.com

# Default compression level (0=disabled, 1-9)
compress: 3

# Allow TURN relay without prompting
allow-relay: false

# Transport mode (auto, tcp, webrtc)
transport: auto

# Default output directory for received files
output: ~/Downloads

# Receive and expanded archive limits (0 = 1 TiB each)
max-receive-bytes: 0
max-extract-bytes: 0

# Always show verbose output
verbose: false
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Send a single file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sp2p send photo.jpg
.fi
.RE
.PP
Send multiple files:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sp2p send file1.txt file2.txt file3.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Send a directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sp2p send ./my-folder
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pipe data from another command:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ tar cf - src/ | sp2p send -name src.tar -
.fi
.RE
.PP
Receive a file using the share code:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sp2p receive abc-def-ghi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Receive to a specific directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sp2p receive -output ~/Downloads abc-def-ghi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pipe received data to another command:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sp2p receive -stdout abc-def-ghi | tar xf -
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use a custom server:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sp2p send -server https://relay.example.com photo.jpg
.fi
.RE
.PP
Send with an agent-readable event stream:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ sp2p send -format json photo.jpg
.fi
.RE
